​
1st Level: Patron's budget
Starting at 1st level, you can use your action to request nonmagical weapons, items, and food to your specific location, these are purchased with a budget the company has allotted you. The company budget is equal to your level plus your proficiency, and it resets either on a long rest. These items are corporate property, and except food, losing them will lead to you needing to pay the exact cost of the item. 
These items are magically transported and must be used for specific short term purposes, and returned when that purpose is served via that same magical teleportation.
They’ll know if you try to sell the food.
​
6th level: Arcane Investment
Starting at 6th level, you can expend a spellslot to return magical energy to your patron in exhange for a boon, after which you may roll on the arcane investment table. you may use a standard action to activate it whenever you wish,
your spellcasting mod will not be used in this roll, for it is a flat roll.
Using a spellslot above 1st level will grant a bonus d4 you can roll alongside the base dice for the final result; if the final result is higher than the dice table, it automatically defaults to the highest number,
most of these last till you decide to try to get a new one.

